    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n103106" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τεράστιος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>monstrous,
			prodigious</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὡς τ. τι
			πεποιηκώς</span> (Bernard. rightly <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὥσπερ
				ἀστεῖόν τι</span>) <i><span class="en">
				Thphr.
				<u>Char.</u>
				19.9
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τ. τι πάσχεις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Luc.
					<u>DMort.</u>
					17.1
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τ. τὸ πρᾶγμα ἐφαίνετο</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Alex.</u>
					16
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τ. σημεῖον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ezek.
					<u>Exag.</u>
					91
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Sm.
				<u>Nu.</u>
				13.34(33)
			</span></i>, al.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τ. ἔργον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ph.
					1.544
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τεράστιοι</span> perh. 
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τερατουργοί</span>
			 in <i><span class="en">
				Rhetor.
			</span></i> in <i><span class="en">
				<u>Cat.Cod.Astr.</u>
				8(4).148
			</span></i>: <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ζεὺς τ</span>. <i>the god of
				portents</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>Tim.</u>
				41
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Aristid.
				2.65
			</span></i>
			<i><span class="en">J.,
				<u>IG</u>5(1).1154</span></i>
				(<span class="entity">Gythium</span>); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δαίμονες τ</span>. <i><span class="en">
				Hld.
				2.5
			</span></i>: <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ τ.,</span>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τέρας</span>
			, <i><span class="en">
				J.
				<u>AJ</u>
				10.2.1
			</span></i>; <i>a monstrous birth</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Paul.Aeg.
				3.76
			</span></i> (pl.). Adv.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ίως</span> Eust.ad <i><span class="en">
				D.P.
				<u>Proll.</u>
				p.79
			</span></i>
			<i><span class="en">
				B.
			</span></i></div>
